+
+## Week 3: the borrowed model
+
+One tap in the top bar and the thread gets summarized into up to three bullets by Gemini Nano,
+the first language model in the app. It is also the first model the app does not own: it lives in
+AICore, an Android system service, and every app on the phone shares the same copy.
+
+```
+app/src/main/java/com/kuza/app
+├── MainActivity.kt                 now also hands the ViewModel a Summarizer
+├── domain/
+│   └── Summarizer.kt               the third seam, Summary (a closed set of five outcomes),
+│                                   SummaryLength, and SummaryRules (the two gates)
+├── ml/
+│   └── GeminiNanoSummarizer.kt     ML Kit GenAI Summarization behind the seam
+└── presentation/
+    ├── ChatViewModel.kt            summary and summarizing in ChatState, Summarize and DismissSummary intents
+    └── ChatScreen.kt               a Summarize action in the top bar and a SummaryCard above the chips
+```
+
+What changed in the build: `com.google.mlkit:genai-summarization:1.0.0-beta1` (beta, no SLA, no
+deprecation policy, unchanged since its first release and still at beta1 in the Oct 26, 2026 ML Kit
+release notes) and `kotlinx-coroutines-guava`, because the GenAI APIs return Guava
+`ListenableFuture` and we want `await()`. The model itself adds nothing to the APK.
+
+Device requirements: Android 8.0+ is the floor, but the feature only runs on phones Google lists
+for the ML Kit GenAI text APIs: Pixel 9 and 10 series, Pixel 11 series, Galaxy S25 and S26 series,
+Galaxy Z Fold7, Fold8 and Flip8, plus a list of Honor, OnePlus, OPPO, POCO, realme, vivo, Xiaomi,
+Motorola, Sony and Sharp devices, and the Googlebook laptops. No Pixel 8, no Galaxy S24, no
+emulator, and no device with an unlocked bootloader. Elsewhere `checkFeatureStatus()` returns
+`UNAVAILABLE` and the card says so. The first use on a supported phone may download the feature
+through AICore; the docs do not publish the size, so the app shows the byte count AICore reports.
+English, Japanese and Korean only; the app asks for English.
+
+House rules that are not ours: inference only while the app is in the foreground
+(`BACKGROUND_USE_BLOCKED` otherwise), a per-app inference quota (`BUSY`), and a per-app daily
+battery quota (`PER_APP_BATTERY_USE_QUOTA_EXCEEDED`). Input is capped at 4000 tokens; the SDK's
+auto truncation keeps the prefix, so `SummaryRules.conversation` trims from the head itself and
+keeps the newest 12000 characters.
+
+Honest note: this week's code was written and reviewed without an Android toolchain or a Gemini
+Nano phone on the machine that wrote it. `SummaryRulesTest` and `ChatViewModelTest` cover the two
+gates and the plumbing; compile verification and the first real summary are on Ali's Pixel before
+the tag. The one thing to check first: `GenAiException.errorCode` and the `DownloadCallback`
+signatures in `GeminiNanoSummarizer`, which were written from the reference docs, not a compiler.
+
+```bash
+./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest     # SummaryRulesTest, SuggestionRulesTest, ChatViewModelTest, ScriptedFriendTest
+```
