+# The Landlord Owns the Bulb
+
+### Ship the model you own. Queue for the model you borrow.
+
+*AI in Mobile, a weekly learning journey across iOS and Android*
+
+---
+
+Last week, in "The First Bulb Lit the Wrong Side of the Table," the first model into Kuza was a 5.7 MB file inside my APK. This week the first language model arrived, and it did not come inside the APK at all. It came with a landlord.
+
+Sit down. Week three adds a Summarize button: one tap and Gemini Nano reads the thread and hands back three bullets. The artifact is `com.google.mlkit:genai-summarization:1.0.0-beta1`, still beta1 in the October 26, 2026 release notes, and it adds zero bytes to the APK. Gemini Nano lives in AICore, an Android system service, and every app on the phone shares one copy, the way one grandmother cooks for the whole compound. You do not bring a pot. You bring a plate and wait your turn.
+
+The seam is the third of its kind, the first that reads the whole table:
+
+```kotlin
+fun interface Summarizer {
+    suspend fun summarize(transcript: List<Message>): Summary
+}
+```
+
+The model wants the thread as a document, `<name>: <message>` one per line, under 4000 tokens. Here is the turn, and it arrived in the first hour. The SDK offers auto truncation for long input, and it keeps the prefix. The prefix of a chat is "hi." So the gate trims from the head itself and keeps the newest 12000 characters:
+
+```kotlin
+var budget = MAX_CHARS
+val kept = ArrayList<String>(lines.size)
+for (line in lines.asReversed()) {
+    budget -= line.length + 1
+    if (budget < 0) break
+    kept += line
+}
+```
+
+Then the landlord's rules, which are not mine. Inference runs only while the app is in the foreground. Each app has an inference quota (`BUSY` past it) and a daily battery quota. The feature exists only on a published list of phones: Pixel 9, 10 and 11, Galaxy S25 and S26, the new folds, and a roll call of Honor, OnePlus, OPPO, Xiaomi and vivo. No Pixel 8. No Galaxy S24. No emulator. Everywhere else the status check says `UNAVAILABLE`. On a supported phone the first use may download the feature, at a size Google does not publish. The callback tells you the number; the documentation does not.
+
+So the summarizer has five answers, and the screen knows each by name:
+
+```kotlin
+sealed interface Summary {
+    data class Bullets(val lines: List<String>) : Summary
+    data object TooShort : Summary
+    data object NotOnThisPhone : Summary
+    data class Downloading(val bytes: Long) : Summary
+    data class Failed(val reason: String) : Summary
+}
+```
+
+Last week the model explained its silence with a status code. This week the operating system explains it with a queue, a meter, and a guest list. Every outcome has words on the card. None is a spinner.
+
+The tradeoffs, told straight. You get a real language model for free: nothing in the APK, no model to update, no GPU memory to manage, and the thread never leaves the phone. You pay in three currencies. Reach: my mother's phone is not on the list, and neither is yours if it is two years old. Control: the Nano version varies by device, so one thread summarizes differently on a Pixel 9 and a Xiaomi 15, and you cannot pin it. Ownership: a quota you did not set can refuse your feature at the busiest hour of the day. If summarizing is a nice touch, this is the right tool and it costs two dependencies. If summarizing is the product, you do not build the product on a borrowed pot.
+
+**The leadership lens.** Ask one question before the team ships a platform model feature: who can turn it off? With a bundled model, you. With AICore: Google, the OEM, the battery, and the phone's age, in that order. Fine for a feature you can hide behind a status check. Not fine for the feature on the pricing page.
+
+Ship the model you own. Queue for the model you borrow.
+
+*Code: github.com/AliZiwa/kuza, tag `week-03`, commit "Week 3: ML Kit GenAI Summarization of the thread behind a Summarizer seam." Compile verification is on Ali's machine. Next week we buy our own pot: Gemma 4 E2B on LiteRT-LM behind the Replier seam, one line changed in MainActivity, and the price arrives in gigabytes.*
+
